{:edb/db-before-t 563 :edb/db-after-t 564 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533876 50 #inst "2026-10-05T06:43:17.898Z" 13194139533876 true] [17592186068681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262882 13194139533876 true] [17592186068682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262889 13194139533876 true] [17592186068682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262896 13194139533876 true] [17592186068682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186262903 13194139533876 true] [17592186069251 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533876 true] [17592186069251 1145 "We wish to add the following fractions:\n\n$$\np+q=\\frac{6y}{5(1-2y)}+\\frac{9-4y}{1-2y}\n$$\n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of $5(1-2y)$ if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6y}{5(1-2y)}+\\frac{9-4y}{1-2y} & = \\\\ \\frac{6y}{5(1-2y)}+\\frac{5}{5}\\cdot \\frac{9-4y}{1-2y} & = \\\\ \\frac{6y}{5(1-2y)}+\\frac{5(9-4y)}{5(1-2y)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6y+5(9-4y)}{5(1-2y)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6y+45-20y}{5(1-2y)} & = \\\\ \\frac{-14y+45}{5(1-2y)} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533876 true] [17592186262882 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262883 13194139533876 true] [17592186262882 1089 "q-113291" 13194139533876 true] [17592186262882 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533876 true] [17592186262882 1100 "Given that $\\frac{5n+3}{n-2}=b$ and $\\frac{2n-1}{2-n}=c,$ what is $b-c?$" 13194139533876 true] [17592186262882 1113 #uuid "c78ad5bb-bc8b-5f94-a2c4-c8f19012e47a" 13194139533876 true] [17592186262882 1145 "We wish to subtract the following fractions:\n\n$$\nb-c=\\frac{5n+3}{n-2}-\\frac{2n-1}{2-n}\n$$\n\nIn order to subtract the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of $n-2$ if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5n+3}{n-2}-\\frac{2n-1}{2-n} & = \\\\ \\frac{5n+3}{n-2}-\\frac{(-1)}{(-1)}\\cdot \\frac{2n-1}{2-n} & = \\\\ \\frac{5n